(:id "c/R30" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t14_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCT14CompressedFloats/c/R30") :note "Partly reconciled 2026-09-19. Two of this task six clauses are now exercised on all nine legs by the rows in :evidence. cfloat_res_refine proves FINER WIDENS: a writer resolution refined by the reader is read whole and lawfully. cfloat_range_widen proves that the compressed float rides as the float through a bounds pass that is the READER own (schema#1164, ruled B): past_cfloat_range_widen.bin forges aim to 5.0, outside the reader [-2, 2] as well as the writer [-1, 1], and a correct leg lands 2.0 with clamped == 1. That row found a REAL DEFECT on four of the nine legs on its first outing — java, dart, js and elixir had no float clamp at all and landed 5.0 with clamped 0 (schema#1190), each fixed in the PR named here. STILL UNPROVEN, and why this task stays :unknown: COARSER REFUSES BY NAME is exercised by no landed row; the step being carried in the digest under tag Q is not asserted by these rows; DROPPING THE TRIPLE WIDENS is not exercised; and FP-CONTRACT OFF ON EVERY LEG is a build-flag claim no row here tests. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-elixir at 6d091ebf55d167d335f074cdecde9329ab6b6ab3; origin/sprint/schema-rust at 1cbd48a24f09b60ca24a82287dfe8b6d14c1a8e0; origin/sprint/schema-shared at 8c67a42b7dd617faf85b41f5a02fd124297161fb (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
(:id "cards/a-cs-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" :state :done :evidence ("tables/cards/cs/Tests/Program.cs: TestUpgradeMatchesGo, TestTaskHashFramesLogicalFields, TestFieldEditLeavesTheTaskHashAlone, TestViewWalksEveryField (RUN and PASS via make cards-cs-test, Debug and Release)" "make cards-cs-conformance requires and passes all nine surfaces (load 4/4, save 4/4, render 4/4, parse 2/2, bounds 12/12, upgrade 5/5, edit 8/8, taskhash 3/3, view 1/1) with no absence" "make cards-cs-conformance-upgrade-negative-control and make cards-cs-conformance-hash-negative-control each go red on their own surface only (upgrade and taskhash), beside the render control") :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: layers L3 and L4 of the card design in C#: an old card upgraded to the current declaration losing nothing, field edits that leave the body and the task hash alone, and the view that walks a record by name and kind, each matching the Go leg on the shared corpus; each function cites the property it keeps from tla/CardVersioning.tla (NoFieldLost, BodyUnchanged, RefusalKeepsOriginal) and tla/CardHops.tla (ImplementationsAgree, TaskHashStable, the reversed witness EditDropsUnknown). Done when make cards-cs-test runs TestUpgradeMatchesGo, TestTaskHashFramesLogicalFields, TestFieldEditLeavesTheTaskHashAlone and TestViewWalksEveryField green, make cards-cs-conformance requires and passes all nine surfaces with no absence, and the upgrade and hash negative controls each go red on their own surface only. Needs: a-cs-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus (open). Order: second of two in schema-vt-cs, after a-cs-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus; needed by the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language. No attempt was dealt; nothing pushed. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-cs (base sprint/schema-finish). Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-cs at c74ce891600184c632c91d21863ea44a27b9ac93 (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
(:id "cards/a-dart-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus" :state :done :evidence ("make cards-dart-test cards-dart-conformance cards-dart-conformance-negative-control (landed 973c391e)") :note "Landed in sprint/schema-dart via 973c391e, with the facade in tables/cards/dart and the make targets cards-dart-test, cards-dart-conformance and the three negative controls. Task: layers L1 and L2 of the card design in Dart: the card record as a generated variable table with an owning facade and the customer bounds, and the brief text parsed once and rendered many times, each matching the Go leg byte for byte on the shared corpus. The facade lives in tables/cards/dart (lib/cards.dart, lib/sha256.dart, bin/driver.dart, test/cards_test.dart and the executable driver script); its calls are the Go facade calls in the language's own spelling. Done when make cards-dart-test runs TestCardRoundTripsThePopulatedFixture, TestCardBoundsRefuseBeforePublishing and TestParseRenderMatchesGo green, make cards-dart-conformance reports pass for load, save, render, parse and bounds, and the negative control goes red on render only. Needs: dart-carries-the-variable-form-for-card-constructs (landed), the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set (landed). Order: first in line in schema-vt-dart; needed by a-dart-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-dart at 0c2cba0631b878a685075a07059ea05f15c19977 (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
