(:id "cpp/E3/fixed-array-element" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedroadmap_t12_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCppT12PlansEvolution/cpp/E3/fixed-array-element") :tested-revision "7f82cdc7bee2a169be2df847a8dd13b6170958fe" :note "NOT reconciled. The evidence recorded before this was a BARE PR URL (#994) naming no file and no test. The row exists on this leg — fixedversioning_test.go carries {row: fixed_I_grow_element, widens: true} — but it carries NO CHECK BODY, so clause one of this title, exact per-slot scaled values, is asserted NOWHERE: nothing compares the landed slots against the expected scaled values. Clause two, older-reader refusal, is not covered either: this leg has no OLD-REFUSES-NEW column, and the suite own comment says so — OLD-REFUSES-NEW is the second column and is not in this suite. The seven legs whose row carries a check body and an OLD-REFUSES-NEW column are :done. What would close it: a check body for this row and an OLD-REFUSES-NEW column on this leg. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-cpp at 9c7edaa095a6c5e51bf1353b32e6d4760cbcf7bf (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
(:id "cpp/E8" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedroadmap_t18_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCppT18FieldEvolution/cpp/E8") :tested-revision "241430c299d6577921768c9cc81bb80826fcc1c8" :note "Historical report at b7ab66a8; current completion has not been reconciled. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-cpp at 9c7edaa095a6c5e51bf1353b32e6d4760cbcf7bf (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
(:id "cpp/R19" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedroadmap_t18_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCppT18FieldEvolution/cpp/R19") :tested-revision "241430c299d6577921768c9cc81bb80826fcc1c8" :note "Partly reconciled 2026-09-19. The union_unselected_arm row in :evidence is a clean NEW-READS-OLD over VOLD_/VNEW_union_append — an APPENDED ARM — and asserts that the read moves NO counter at all: retained, retain_lost, widened, unknown, kind_mismatch, clamped and duplicate are each exactly 0 while the tag lands the writer alpha arm and its payload lands the writer 7. That is this task appended-ARM kind, on all nine legs, under schema#1157 ruled LAWFUL AS IS. STILL UNPROVEN, and why this task stays :unknown: the title names five kinds and only one is covered — a clean NEW-READS-OLD of an appended FIELD, an appended VARIANT, an appended FLAG and an appended KEYED SLOT each still want a row. The landed rows that touch those shapes are hostile ones (a forged ordinal, a forged count, a forged hash), and a hostile read is not the clean read this clause is about. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-cpp at 9c7edaa095a6c5e51bf1353b32e6d4760cbcf7bf (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
(:id "cpp/R30" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedroadmap_t14_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCppT14CompressedFloats/cpp/R30") :note "Partly reconciled 2026-09-19. Two of this task six clauses are now exercised on all nine legs by the rows in :evidence. cfloat_res_refine proves FINER WIDENS: a writer resolution refined by the reader is read whole and lawfully. cfloat_range_widen proves that the compressed float rides as the float through a bounds pass that is the READER own (schema#1164, ruled B): past_cfloat_range_widen.bin forges aim to 5.0, outside the reader [-2, 2] as well as the writer [-1, 1], and a correct leg lands 2.0 with clamped == 1. That row found a REAL DEFECT on four of the nine legs on its first outing — java, dart, js and elixir had no float clamp at all and landed 5.0 with clamped 0 (schema#1190), each fixed in the PR named here. STILL UNPROVEN, and why this task stays :unknown: COARSER REFUSES BY NAME is exercised by no landed row; the step being carried in the digest under tag Q is not asserted by these rows; DROPPING THE TRIPLE WIDENS is not exercised; and FP-CONTRACT OFF ON EVERY LEG is a build-flag claim no row here tests. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-elixir at 6d091ebf55d167d335f074cdecde9329ab6b6ab3; origin/sprint/schema-rust at 1cbd48a24f09b60ca24a82287dfe8b6d14c1a8e0; origin/sprint/schema-shared at 8c67a42b7dd617faf85b41f5a02fd124297161fb (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
(:id "cpp/R9/seven-corruptions" :state :done :evidence ("test/tables/fixedform_main.cpp: layout_validation() through refuses(), run by make tables-fixedform") :tested-revision "7f82cdc7bee2a169be2df847a8dd13b6170958fe" :note "NOT reconciled, and THE CITATION WAS WRONG. The evidence recorded before this was the single URL #1002, whose diff contains no occurrence of corrupt or seven and which touches ci-fast.yml, internal/ci/fast_plan_test.go and test/tables/versioning_numbers.cpp. The real test exists and predates it: layout_validation() in test/tables/fixedform_main.cpp drives TWELVE cases of refuses( f, tblfx1::layout_malformed, 'RULE: ...' ) over a KNOWN hash whose layout bytes differ — the entry count, a zero count, a kind outside the closed set, a TABLE root, a constant size its kind does not admit, a table size that is not the sum of its fields, the tree running out of layout, the layout outlasting the tree, a record past 65536, a size that would overflow the sum, a depth past the walk bound, and a file shorter than a header — which covers clause one, the seven §1.1 breaks, and more. The refuses() helper also asserts r.unknown, r.kind_mismatch, r.widened and r.clamped are all zero with malformed false, which is clause three, CLEAR COUNTERS. CLAUSE TWO, PRESERVE DESTINATION, IS ASSERTED NOWHERE: refuses() constructs its own FxRoot, resets it, passes it to the load and never inspects it afterwards, so a refusal that half-wrote the destination would pass every one of the twelve cases. That is the damage the clause exists to prevent, and it is the one thing this row does not read. What would close it: poison the destination before the load and sweep it after, as §5.8 row 9 does on the six legs that carry it. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-cpp at 9c7edaa095a6c5e51bf1353b32e6d4760cbcf7bf (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
