(:id "vt/c/generator-panic" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t18_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCT18DirectArms (union-field-arms/c/valid-data, vt/c/generator-panic)" "make tables-c SERIALIZE_C=<serialize.c v1.10.0, the ci-full.yml pin> NODE=node (26.x, the js.mk override): exit 0, wire-fuzz 0 divergences; grep -rn table_fixed_put0 build/tables-generated-c/ prints nothing") :tested-revision "2d91bb71a7d0d665b06f3e56beab06aff1858094" :note "DONE: make tables-c ran green at 2d91bb71a with the serialize.c sibling staged at its pinned tag v1.10.0 (Rowan's hand run, 2026-10-14, darwin/arm64 clang). HISTORY, the red this leaf held: THE CODE RED IS FIXED, the red that remains is the absent serialize.c sibling. The R2.schema nil-arm panic and the direct-arm table_fixed_put0 gap are both fixed: internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go now carries an emitFixedWriteArm twin of the reference (internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedform.go:473) routing text, bytes and array arms through the arm's own unnamed struct, and the union case of emitFixedWriteElement calls it; TestFixedCT18DirectArmLines and TestFixedRoadmapCT18DirectArms/vt/c/generator-panic are green, and `grep -rn table_fixed_put0 build/tables-generated-c/` prints nothing after make build/tables-generated-c/.stamp. The next red is the ENVIRONMENT PREREQUISITE, not a code line: `make tables-c SERIALIZE_C=../serialize.c` stops at build/tables-generated-c/scalars/ScalarsTable.h:32: fatal error: serialize.h: No such file or directory (also scalars2/Scalars2Table.h:32, test/conformance/c/unit_scalars.c:2, test/conformance/c/unit_tblscalars2.c:1) because the serialize.c sibling checkout is absent in this worktree; every other conformance translation unit compiles clean under -Werror -Wshadow. The member must stage the serialize.c sibling and run `make tables-c SERIALIZE_C=<the staged sibling>`; when that run is green this leaf flips :done. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-c at 310e99207099374a856340e548721bff0756a661 (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
