(:id "vt/cook-write/rust" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/rusttable/blockbuild_test.go TestBlockBuildAndCookWriteRust: <T>_cook_measure, <T>_cook_measure_reason and <T>_cook_from(value, buffer, order), the measure recomputed from the same ir as gotable/cookwrite.go (64 + round(size, max(8, align)) + 16), both byte orders, the short-buffer refusal before any byte changes, the trailer's table wire id, and TableCookRefuse answering as TableRefuseInvalidValue does" "make tables-rust-block-build (in make test-rust)" "test/conformance/rust/src/main.rs: surface_cook_write (make conformance)") :tested-revision "473585fa01c5" :note "RUN at 473585fa01c5 plus this change, on the bench: the FIXED path only, proved by TestBlockBuildAndCookWriteRust. The conformance driver answers EVERY cook-write row .absent, and the reason is upstream of it: the emitted runtime carries the cook WRITER (<T>_cook_measure, <T>_cook_measure_reason, <T>_cook_from) but NO form-1 (id-table) WIRE reader <T>_load for a FIXED table — its only fixed reader is <T>_fixed_load, which reads form 3 — so surface_cook_write cannot turn testdata/wire/tables/<case>.bin into a value to cook. Every row stays absent waiting on rust-carries-the-fixed-class-on-the-table-wire (vt/fixed-class/rust), which ports the form-1 (id-table) WIRE reader <T>_load for a FIXED table (gotable/read.go's emitTableRead) and then drives <T>_cook_from for WideBlob and KeyedConfig; the variable-class graph_* rows additionally need the variable region writer (numbering, containers), not carried. Until then every cook-write row stays absent, each named here with its big-endian half: root_full, root_full-be, root_default, root_default-be, profile_elide, profile_elide-be, loadout_full, loadout_full-be, wide_blob, wide_blob-be, archive, archive-be, keyed_config, keyed_config-be, keyed_default, keyed_default-be, v1_cfg, v1_cfg-be, v1_seams, v1_seams-be, v2_cfg, v2_cfg-be, v2_seams, v2_seams-be, chain_value, chain_value-be, chain_value_empty, chain_value_empty-be, chain_optional, chain_optional-be, chain_optional_empty, chain_optional_empty-be, graph_tree, graph_tree-be, graph_shared, graph_shared-be, graph_empty, graph_empty-be, graph_deep, graph_deep-be, message_open, message_open-be, message_transaction, message_transaction-be, message_ping, message_ping-be, message_save, message_save-be, message_empty, message_empty-be, message_batch, message_batch-be, message_arms, message_arms-be, message_arm_edits, message_arm_edits-be, message_ack, message_ack-be, message_trace, message_trace-be, m1_open, m1_open-be, m2_open, m2_open-be, stream_chain, stream_chain-be, stream_header, stream_header-be, stream_parts, stream_parts-be, stream_arm_first, stream_arm_first-be, stream_arm_pointer, stream_arm_pointer-be, blob_small, blob_small-be, blob_empty, blob_empty-be, blob_large, blob_large-be, blob_shared, blob_shared-be, blob_str8, blob_str8-be, blob_str16, blob_str16-be, scalars_full, scalars_full-be, scalars_default, scalars_default-be, scalars_edges, scalars_edges-be. Proved by landed sprint work on the stream base: origin/sprint/schema-rust at 1cbd48a24f09b60ca24a82287dfe8b6d14c1a8e0 (carried to main's overlay 2026-10-19).")
